    "narrative": "As we push through the heat of the 2026 campaign, our lineup is primed to exploit some exploitable arms today, led by **Corbin Carroll**, who sits at our highest efficiency score of 79.66. **Corbin Carroll** draws a favorable matchup against Abbott, who carries an xERA of 5.01; despite the platoon disadvantage, his natural ceiling and the elevated scoring environment of his park make him our anchor. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** is a strong start (72.92) as he faces Waguespack. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits significantly from a high-efficiency right-on-right matchup where his contact profile should thrive, driving his score up nearly 15% based on SP skill alone.\n\nOur focus on stolen bases remains a tactical priority, making **Brice Turang** (63.57) and **Gabriel Moreno** (66.83) essential staples of today\u2019s construction. While **Brice Turang** earns an 8% boost for his spot in the two-hole, **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from a massive 19% bump due to the soft matchup against Abbott. The most difficult decision at the margins involved **Isaac Paredes**, who just missed the cut with a 43.29 score. While **Isaac Paredes** provides a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Mickey Moniak** (54.67), whose 14% park-factor surge against the lefty Griffin outweighs the marginal utility of **Isaac Paredes** facing a tough Imanaga.\n\nWe are monitoring the lower end of the order, specifically **Griffin Conine** (44.43) and **Austin Riley** (48.23). **Griffin Conine** is walking a thin line against Kent; though his xwOBA remains healthy, his platoon-neutral efficiency is heavily suppressed by the spot in the lineup. Likewise, **Austin Riley** is seeing his value hampered by an 8th-order slot, making him a marginal play. We remain sidelined on the injury front with **Trevor Story** and **James Wood**, whose absence continues to thin our bench depth. We are banking on **Corbin Carroll** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** to carry the heavy lifting while hoping **Seiya Suzuki** can utilize his 85% stolen base situational efficiency to create separation in our scarcest category.",
